  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is an equilateral triangle.</p><p>Let the side of the triangle be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>Perpendicular distance from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;to the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1039cd7b-7b65-465c-a0c4-42ed4e8d1724-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mi>a</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
